<article class="env-remark" id="04KP">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04KP">Remark <span data-tag="04KP">11.9.2.11</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category containing a pushout square </p>
<div class="equation" id="06Y2">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="06Y2" href="/tag/06Y2">11.18</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:w-local-pushout} \xymatrix@C =50pt@R=50pt{ X \ar [d] \ar [r]^{w} &amp;  Y \ar [d] \\ X' \ar [r]^{w'} &amp;  Y'. } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> If an object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is $w$-local, then it is also $w'$-local. To see this, let $h_{C}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ be the functor represented by the object $C$. Applying the functor $h_{C}$ to (<a data-tag="06Y2" href="/tag/06Y2">11.18</a>), we obtain a pullback diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \xymatrix@C =50pt@R=50pt{ \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X,C) &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(Y,C) \ar [l] \\ \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(X',C) \ar [u] &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(Y',C) \ar [u] \ar [l] } \]
</div>
<p> in the $\infty $-category of spaces $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ (Corollary <a data-tag="039M" href="/tag/039M">7.4.1.23</a>). Our assumption that $C$ is $w$-local guarantees the upper horizontal map is an isomorphism, so the lower horizontal map is also an isomorphism (Corollary <a data-tag="048F" href="/tag/048F">7.6.2.39</a>). </p>
</article>
